#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:3
#: 4160384ea99d4aff8170c1d00dc4bacb
msgid "How to edit the documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:5
#: 3f617724d59e43ee878628a10f258ced
msgid ""
"The Qubes OS documentation is stored as `reStructuredText (rST) <https://"
"docutils.sourceforge.io/rst.html>`__ files in the `qubes-doc <https://"
"github.com/QubesOS/qubes-doc>`__ repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:8
#: 201e467183cf49a2b3c071aced009033
msgid ""
"We use `Sphinx <https://www.sphinx-doc.org/>`__ for building and `Read The "
"Docs (RTD) <https://about.readthedocs.com/>`__ for hosting. RTD is a "
"`continuous‑documentation deployment platform <https://docs.readthedocs.com/"
"platform/stable/continuous-deployment.html>`__ that can automatically detect "
"changes in a GitHub repository and build the latest version of a "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:13
#: 93fc094540954e73beed5208de11799f
msgid ""
"Qubes OS Documentation Workflow - once new documentation is written or "
"changed, it is built and verified with Sphinx, pushed on GitHub/GitLab and "
"hosted on RTD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:19
#: 05c3849f5bfd48c68f9a84ffb5b8b7f9
msgid ""
"By cloning and regularly pulling from `qubes-doc <https://github.com/QubesOS/"
"qubes-doc>`__ repository, users can maintain their own up-to-date offline "
"copy of the Qubes documentation rather than relying solely on the web and "
"either serve it locally or read the rST files directly. EPUB or PDF versions "
"of Qubes OS documentation can also be downloaded from `doc.qubes-os.org "
"<https://doc.qubes-os.org/en/latest/>`__:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:25
#: 09ea131f5c194e3a8fdb3003c1f438ea
msgid ""
"Highlights from where one can download a ePUB or PDF of hte Qubes OS "
"documentation deployed on RTD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:31
#: b5f6da7c805942279848515b3790a3d7
msgid ""
"The documentation is a volunteer community effort. People like you are "
"constantly working to make it better. If you notice something that can be "
"fixed or improved, please follow the steps below to open a pull request!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:38
#: 915af231a67a4417ade773ff334e7cf8
msgid "How to submit a pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:40
#: a175c4869f024482b2839fb50d6f9e4f
msgid ""
"We keep all the rST documentation in `qubes-doc <https://github.com/QubesOS/"
"qubes-doc>`__, a dedicated Git repository hosted on `GitHub <https://"
"github.com/>`__. Thanks to GitHub’s easy web interface, you can edit the "
"documentation even if you’re not familiar with Git or the command line! All "
"you need is a free GitHub account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:46
#: 2fb95cf94805472a95210d7728c7d8d2
msgid "A few notes before we get started:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:48
#: 9c04527b70b4411782bb037b3e06fddc
msgid ""
"Since Qubes is a security-oriented project, every documentation change will "
"be :ref:`reviewed <developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-"
"documentation:security>` before it’s accepted. This allows us to maintain "
"quality control and protect our users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:50
#: d70bc4b0600344d6acf0f55abd20b271
msgid ""
"To give your contribution a better chance of being accepted, please follow "
"our :doc:`/developer/general/rst-documentation-style-guide`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:52
#: d9f835538b4a4830bf6c7ad2f7888db9
msgid ""
"We don’t want you to spend time and effort on a contribution that we can’t "
"accept. If your contribution would take a lot of time, please :doc:`file an "
"issue </introduction/issue-tracking>` for it first so that we can make sure "
"we’re on the same page before significant works begins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:54
#: b0ddcc0003ce4d56abaa8676f3de3909
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you may already have written content that doesn’t conform to "
"these guidelines, but you’d be willing to modify it so that it does. In this "
"case, you can still submit it by following the instructions below. Just make "
"a note in your pull request (PR) that you’re aware of the changes that need "
"to be made and that you’re just asking for the content to be reviewed before "
"you spend time making those changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:56
#: 04c3a77d4b994857babb97052b81ea1a
msgid ""
"Finally, if you’ve written something that doesn’t belong in qubes-doc but "
"that would be beneficial to the Qubes community, please consider adding it "
"to the :ref:`external documentation <developer/general/rst-documentation-"
"style-guide:core vs. external documentation>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-documentation.rst:58
#: 8383c8fb8eb44f298a9d8db6b0a56937
msgid ""
"(**Advanced users:** If you’re already familiar with GitHub or wish to work "
"from the command line, you can skip the rest of this section. All you need "
"to do to contribute is to `fork and clone <https://guides.github.com/"
"activities/forking/>`__ the `qubes-doc <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-"
"doc>`__ repo, make your changes, then `submit a pull request <https://"
"help.github.com/articles/using-pull-requests/>`__. You can continue "
"reading :ref:`viewing_pr`.)"
msgstr ""

